# ThreadSanitizer suppressions (CLAUDE.md, "Sanitizers"). Run with
#   TSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=tests/tsan.supp
#
# SQLite's WAL index ("-shm", shared memory) is read without locks by design: connections
# coordinate through file locks (fcntl) and memory barriers, which ThreadSanitizer doesn't
# see. Two connections writing in turn (one per drive worker) then look like a race inside
# these functions. Only SQLite's own wal-index functions are listed, so races in hoardor's
# code still show.
race:walIndexWriteHdr
race:walIndexTryHdr
race:walIndexReadHdr
race:walTryBeginRead
race:walIndexAppend
race:walCheckpoint
